decision: pass
reviewer: claude-opus-5-5 (self-review)
audience: Technical leads and maintainers
purpose: Why does the standard carry no default branch names?

Records the removal of branch-defaults: the standard holds no branch names, and tools give no answer when roles are undeclared; supersedes the defaults part of ADR 0014.
Translated from Korean to English as a frozen record; the hotfix-prefix fallback rule and the public-ai-qa example are preserved.
Headings mapped to Decision / Context and constraints / Rationale and alternatives / Consequences.
All identifiers (branch-defaults, vcs.branch.model, roles, prefixes.hotfix, check-settings, base-branch, init --detect) kept verbatim; no Korean literals retained.
Tense kept as in the source ("There was one constraint") to match the historical record.

